Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.66,0:00:05.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Edward-sama! \NIs something the matter?!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.60,0:00:07.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's nothing!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.15,0:00:09.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I told them not to disturb us...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.93,0:00:11.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I guess they don't trust you.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.17,0:00:15.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You'd feel a lot better after revealing who you really are, wouldn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.79,0:00:21.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fletcher!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.50,0:00:27.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Run! Hurry!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.23,0:00:30.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.35,0:00:34.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If they catch you, \Nwe won't get off easily, either!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.68,0:00:37.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In time, I'll clear everything up!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.51,0:00:42.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al, let's go!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.40,0:00:58.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.30,0:01:00.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.04,0:01:09.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Man cannot obtain anything \Nwithout first sacrificing something.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.75,0:01:14.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to obtain anything, \Nsomething of equal value is required.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.03,0:01:19.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is alchemy's \NLaw of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.75,0:01:25.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the time, we believed that \Nto be the true way of the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.99,0:03:18.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You promised not to use alchemy, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.00,0:03:19.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dad didn't like it, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.62,0:03:24.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Th-This is terrible!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.82,0:03:26.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mugear-sama...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.63,0:03:29.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You two are all right!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.35,0:03:31.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And the stone? \NIs the stone all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.56,0:03:34.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not to worry, it's right here.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.75,0:03:39.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've done well \Nto make it so large.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.34,0:03:42.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, we don't \Nhave any more time.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.31,0:03:45.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please start using \Nthat other method.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.06,0:03:48.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We don't need to use that method for the stone to—
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.10,0:03:51.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you saying you won't follow my orders?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.14,0:03:53.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,N-No...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.58,0:03:58.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There was once another man who told me the same thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.00,0:04:00.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In the end, he ran away, \Nlike a beaten dog.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.05,0:04:03.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.09,0:04:07.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,With this, even without being an alchemist, I can do this!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.92,0:04:17.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mugear-sama!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.36,0:04:19.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Magnificent!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.73,0:04:25.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The real Elric brothers are said to \Nhave blond hair and golden eyes,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.77,0:04:28.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,sons of Nash Tringham!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.84,0:04:42.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Things have sure been bustling over at the mansion, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.01,0:04:45.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, really?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.10,0:04:46.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You went there again, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.89,0:04:48.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's no helping you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.14,0:04:52.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? Is Elisa still here?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.28,0:04:54.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm. The grapevine is withering,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.26,0:04:57.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so she wanted to stay here, and she won't listen to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.36,0:05:00.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But her cough is terrible.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.27,0:05:02.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I just put her down.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.00,0:05:07.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Red water?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.45,0:05:11.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They're condensing it, \Ntrying to turn it into a stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.20,0:05:13.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then again, compared to the Philosopher's Stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.52,0:05:16.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the red-water piece is \Njust a pale imitation.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.15,0:05:19.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do you suppose he meant by "his father's dream"?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.99,0:05:22.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Probably just some goofy excuse.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.54,0:05:24.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Could it be that those two are...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.47,0:05:26.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nash's sons?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.38,0:05:27.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nash?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.23,0:05:31.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean Nash Tringham, \Nthe discoverer of the red water?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.98,0:05:34.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He was from this town.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.15,0:05:38.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He went to Central to \Nresearch the red water.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.16,0:05:41.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But then, one day, \Nhe came back to this town.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.90,0:05:48.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nash? Well, if it isn't Nash!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.54,0:05:51.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've returned, huh? \NHow are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.87,0:05:56.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This town is completely \Non the decline.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.86,0:06:00.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I think we should stop relying on gold for our way of life.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.24,0:06:05.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How's your research \Non the red water?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.54,0:06:06.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is it coming along?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.72,0:06:11.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I gave up. \NI'll never research it again.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.48,0:06:13.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm not going back to Central, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.89,0:06:16.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What? What about your family?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.66,0:06:19.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm a failure,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.44,0:06:22.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,both as a husband and a father.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.23,0:06:24.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nash...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.09,0:06:28.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He'd abandoned everything he had.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.84,0:06:32.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He wouldn't tell me anything about what happened in Central.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.75,0:06:40.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But then the big landowner in \Nthis town—Mugear—came calling.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.23,0:06:44.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He approached Nash about \Nhis research on the red water.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.44,0:06:49.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No matter how many times you come see me, my answer is the same!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.33,0:06:52.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're saying you'd turn your back on this town?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.80,0:06:56.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right now, the only thing that can produce gold is your red water!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.23,0:06:59.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As long as we have gold, \Nthe town will come back to life!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.46,0:07:04.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nash-san, you're the only one \Nwho can save this town! Please!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.94,0:07:11.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In the end, he secluded himself inside Mugear's mine, and began to research.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.13,0:07:17.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The town once again flourished because of the gold.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.44,0:07:22.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The furnaces were aflame, goods filled the streets,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.63,0:07:25.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and life returned to the people.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.35,0:07:30.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, at the same time, an illness of unknown origin began to spread.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.73,0:07:38.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Without anyone knowing \Nhow to treat it,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.72,0:07:44.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,many, many babies \Ndied soon after birth.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.84,0:07:49.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And Elisa was born around then?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.73,0:07:56.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Shortly, an alchemist doctor named Marcoh wandered into town.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.26,0:08:07.00,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,The cause of this is a toxic material called \Nred water, which has seeped into the ground.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.01,0:08:16.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It glowed?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.51,0:08:17.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.37,0:08:20.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That light... Could it have been...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.57,0:08:26.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In any case, we can be sure that \Nthanks to his treatment, Elisa survived.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.69,0:08:29.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I hounded Nash.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.65,0:08:34.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Answer me, Nash! If this keeps up, this will become a town of death!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.99,0:08:36.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What the hell have you done?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.77,0:08:39.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I was in the wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.07,0:08:43.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Again... Once again...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.82,0:08:47.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to end it all.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.60,0:08:49.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,End it...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.53,0:08:52.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nash...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.88,0:08:56.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After that, no one \Never saw him again.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.10,0:08:59.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Gradually, they couldn't get any more gold,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.30,0:09:01.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and the town once again declined.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.74,0:09:06.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If those two are Nash's sons,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.75,0:09:09.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,they must have come after their father.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.00,0:09:11.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.90,0:09:12.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.40,0:09:17.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They had no choice. The only thing those two have is their father.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.45,0:09:21.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They're just using their pop as \Njustification for what they're doing.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.96,0:09:24.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Maybe so...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.29,0:09:26.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But aren't we doing \Nsomething similar?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.54,0:09:32.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know how those two feel.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.31,0:09:43.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For crying out loud!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.84,0:09:46.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All you had to do was shut up \Nand use that other method...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.28,0:09:49.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother? What method does he mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.80,0:09:51.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's simple, really.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.73,0:09:55.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Have newly pregnant women drink the red water.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.82,0:09:59.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Soon, the water will pass through the placenta and condense...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.25,0:10:00.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.20,0:10:00.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.95,0:10:04.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the right time, you get it from them and transmute it into a stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.31,0:10:08.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a simple, reliable method.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.25,0:10:15.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My, my, you've got the same sissy streak as your father.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.75,0:10:16.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.03,0:10:18.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I just want you to \Ntell me one thing!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.60,0:10:22.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Did Dad use that method?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.36,0:10:27.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hmph, at the last moment, he weaseled out.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.47,0:10:30.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If only he had done it, \Nhis life would've been spared.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.20,0:10:34.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why, you... You said \NDad died from illness!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.30,0:10:37.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wait! Hey, wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.04,0:10:42.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've taken care of everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.85,0:10:47.70,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Now we just have to use the real Elric brothers and put everything into action.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.59,0:10:52.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I doubt it will go that smoothly. \NThey can be very difficult to deal with.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.95,0:10:58.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,One or two kids won't be any \Ntrouble at all! Now, please wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.22,0:11:00.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please wait for \Njust a while longer.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.37,0:11:03.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Very well. Go on.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.08,0:11:10.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}The time for this place is nigh.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.54,0:11:16.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}I'm so sorry about \Nthose two impostors.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.62,0:11:20.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I, too, was completely \Ntaken in by them.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.49,0:11:24.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I feel terrible about \Nadding to our impertinence,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.75,0:11:27.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but seeing as how the two of you are among the finest alchemists of our age,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.87,0:11:30.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,there is a matter that I would like to request your assistance with.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.42,0:11:32.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Research on the red water?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.21,0:11:36.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh! You know about it? \NThat will save me time explaining.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.21,0:11:39.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The truth is, I happened to overhear
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.72,0:11:43.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that you are greatly interested in the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.22,0:11:49.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do you think? It was made by condensing the red water.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.04,0:11:51.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You might call it a trial product for a Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.94,0:11:53.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What am I supposed \Nto do with it now?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.56,0:11:56.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I want to save Xenotime.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.65,0:12:00.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If I can regenerate the gold vein, \Nno one will have to give up on this town!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.49,0:12:02.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I get it.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.69,0:12:04.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, where are the impostors?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.93,0:12:06.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They're being held in \Nan underground cell.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.25,0:12:11.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wh-What are you doing?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.75,0:12:14.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm not interested in \Nany unfinished goods.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.14,0:12:16.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Executing the impostors comes first.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.01,0:12:19.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm not the type of person who forgives liars.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.38,0:12:23.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh! Then you're accepting my request?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.37,0:12:26.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,With us working on it, \Nthis will be child's play.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.21,0:12:28.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Never mind that, I haven't \Nexecuted anyone in a while!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.70,0:12:30.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm just itching for the chance!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.01,0:12:32.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Gonna come watch?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.10,0:12:34.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, I, uh...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.69,0:12:36.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll pass on that.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.59,0:12:44.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.47,0:12:48.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.30,0:12:49.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Alphonse-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.14,0:12:54.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I heard that Nash Tringham was your pop.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.10,0:12:57.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What were you trying to do by carrying on his research?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.30,0:13:01.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.82,0:13:03.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,is Dad's water.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.18,0:13:06.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was my duty to \Ncontinue his research.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.93,0:13:09.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You are such a naïve bastard.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.90,0:13:14.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you know what the people in town are going through because of that toxic water?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.73,0:13:17.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your pop knew.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.77,0:13:20.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's why he tried to \Ngive up his research.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.70,0:13:25.56,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,You can't obtain happiness by relying on the likes of red water or a Philosopher's Stone!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.49,0:13:33.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Move forward! \NDon't act so shamefully!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.60,0:13:36.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not now that you've \Ntaken on my name.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.60,0:13:38.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al! Let's go!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.09,0:13:48.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who cares? As long as the research is successful, those guys will be—
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.34,0:13:51.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those guys? \NWho are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.44,0:13:53.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Something's been bothering me.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.97,0:13:58.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wherever did the red-water \Nresearcher Nash Tringham go?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.02,0:14:03.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nash? Ah, his research wasn't going so well, so I fired him.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.78,0:14:07.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh? You don't seem like someone \Nso good-natured as to let somebody
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.84,0:14:09.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,who knew everything \Nget away from you.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.14,0:14:13.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you trying to say?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.29,0:14:17.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm saying that I don't help murderers out, Mugear!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.92,0:14:20.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why, you!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.76,0:14:22.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In that case, you're not \Ngetting out of here alive!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.79,0:14:25.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can get any number of \Nother alchemists instead!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.96,0:14:26.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A stone?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.72,0:14:28.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There wasn't just that one?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.71,0:14:31.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It may not be as complete as that other one...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.55,0:14:36.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Die!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.23,0:14:40.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you done yet?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.73,0:14:43.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.31,0:14:47.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's plenty more \Nwhere that came from!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.53,0:14:52.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're kidding!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.39,0:15:01.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's useless! Useless!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.06,0:15:08.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Equivalent exchange, my ass! Dammit!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.90,0:15:13.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm not done yet!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.41,0:15:16.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is this?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.23,0:15:21.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now, Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.95,0:15:36.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed! Looks like you needed my help after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.41,0:15:37.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.84,0:15:42.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've given up \Nchasing after our dad.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.93,0:15:46.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're going to go \Nfind our own way.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.32,0:15:49.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.98,0:15:52.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.90,0:15:56.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A secret passage?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.91,0:15:58.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That bastard, he got away!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.96,0:16:03.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Russell, how much farther?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.40,0:16:06.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're almost there! There's a spring where the red water comes out!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.82,0:16:13.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That miserable Mugear! He blocked our way!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.82,0:16:15.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna drag him out of there!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.50,0:16:21.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.27,0:16:26.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll never surrender the spring!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.00,0:16:29.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As long as I have this water, I can continue researching!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.07,0:16:33.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm not afraid of \Nany State Alchemist!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.51,0:16:35.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.44,0:16:36.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.22,0:16:40.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now you've said it, Mugear! \NDon't you mock the State Alchemists!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.39,0:16:42.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Die!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.61,0:16:52.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you see now?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.11,0:16:54.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm on an entirely \Ndifferent level than you!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.84,0:16:59.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.04,0:17:06.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed! That's enough! \NLet's get out of here!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.28,0:17:07.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.52,0:17:12.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I won't give up this spring!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.10,0:17:28.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's the water! \NThe red water is overflowing!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.43,0:17:34.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That should hold it for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.98,0:17:36.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are the other places all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.70,0:17:41.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The bedrock will be unstable after that shock. Let's go!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.56,0:18:01.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now, if we can just \Nstop it from coming out...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.83,0:18:27.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The trees...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.14,0:18:29.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They're absorbing the red water!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.46,0:18:32.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, these kinds of trees \Nwere in the laboratory as well!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.36,0:18:36.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You had them absorb the red water to detoxify it?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.77,0:18:41.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.15,0:19:12.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those guys did it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.38,0:19:22.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thanks. Sorry about this.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.10,0:20:08.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Here. These are from Belsio-san.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.18,0:20:10.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thanks!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.44,0:20:12.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Big Brother, take care!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.36,0:20:13.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come see us again!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.94,0:20:15.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Mm-hmm, we'll come again for sure!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.18,0:20:17.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You sure you can get by in this town?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.98,0:20:17.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Really? Promise?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.40,0:20:20.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We'll accept whatever's coming to us.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.47,0:20:22.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Okay, let's do a parting handshake!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.58,0:20:23.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Working with Belsio-san, my powers will be useful.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.62,0:20:29.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed, are you still going to search for the Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.62,0:20:27.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Wow, you're so big!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.40,0:20:35.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.36,0:20:40.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Look, how about I tell you \Nhow to condense a red stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.67,0:20:41.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.48,0:20:44.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not by way of apology,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.43,0:20:47.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,it's just that I think \Nyou should know.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.81,0:20:52.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We don't need that stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.29,0:20:55.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We'll find it on our own.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.59,0:20:57.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Count on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.12,0:21:01.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed-san! Please come again! \NWe're sure to make this town better!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.07,0:21:04.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When you do, Big Brother, \Nbe taller, okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.65,0:21:08.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?! Why, you! \NThat wasn't very nice!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.29,0:21:17.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good-bye!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.54,0:21:19.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Bye-bye!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.00,0:21:21.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good-bye!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.00,0:21:21.50,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,Good-bye!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.78,0:21:24.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good-bye!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.22,0:21:38.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A letter, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.23,0:21:39.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A letter?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.23,0:21:41.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah. What could it be?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.66,0:21:45.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.72,0:21:47.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I-It's nothing!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.24,0:21:53.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Show me! Show me! Show me!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.49,0:21:56.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Show me, already! \NCome on, Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.08,0:21:56.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}"Ed,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.65,0:22:01.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}thanks for all your help."
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.25,0:22:04.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}"Being a year younger than you, \NI'm sorry I was such a smart-aleck."
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.78,0:22:08.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}"I'm trying to be a better \Nolder brother to Fletcher,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:09.53,0:22:11.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and I'll try hard to follow your example, Ed."
Dialogue: 0,0:22:12.09,0:22:13.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}"Well, have a nice trip."
Dialogue: 0,0:22:13.95,0:22:14.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}"Russell."
Dialogue: 0,0:22:16.18,0:22:22.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Damn, how can he be younger than me, \Nand still be taller? What a joke!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:22.06,0:22:24.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those two are going \Nto be all right, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:24.96,0:22:29.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah. They had a nice, \Nresolute look on their faces.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.64,0:23:40.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.40,0:23:43.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 13: "Flame VS Fullmetal"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.77,0:23:46.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel Roy Mustang, State Alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:46.82,0:23:48.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Title: "Flame."
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.56,0:23:50.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's probably stronger than Brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:50.58,0:23:51.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, no he's not!
